<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani money market rates dip on excess funds.</title>
<headline>Pakistani money market rates dip on excess funds.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani money market rates dipped after a net inflow of about two billion rupees in a bonds auction settlement and maturity on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The rates are likely to go up as the central bank has announced a special open market operation for Sunday, one dealer said.</p>
<p>The overnight rates were traded in the band of two and three percent, the dealer said.</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
